From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DeconCrtc <deconcrtc@exynos7580>
Date: Sun, 23 Nov 2026 09:45:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] decon: vendor KMS export shim, attach path and late fb0
 registration

Reuse contract: code/gpu31/kms/decon_api.h (installed as
include/linux/exynos_decon_kms.h, added here verbatim).

The DECON window engine is fbdev-owned today.  A DRM/KMS subdriver needs the
same hardware without dragging fb_info, ION or Android sync_fence into
drivers/gpu/drm, so this patch adds the shim the DECON KMS plan (slice 3/10)
specifies.  No vendor behaviour changes: every entry point either wraps an
existing function or replays the steps the vendor probe/fbdev paths perform.

Layering
  layer A decon_kms_*      stable fb-free surface: attach/detach, enable/
                           disable, one-shot commit from DMA addresses,
                           queued commit with a vendor fence, vblank callback,
                           runtime PM, exporter-agnostic dma-buf mapping.
  layer B decon_export_*   raw vendor symbols, prototypes as in the contract
                           header, EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL (the DECON driver is
                           built-in, so the exports are inert today but make
                           CONFIG_DRM=m and modprobe-free debugging possible).

Address-based window programming
  decon_export_regs_param_addr() is the missing half of decon_set_win_buffer():
  it fills buf_start/whole_w/whole_h/offset_x/offset_y/wincon/blendeq/vidosd_*
  and dma_buf_data[][].dma_addr from caller-owned DMA addresses, with the same
  validation (format, blending, no blending on window 0, dst geometry,
  "window >= 128 bytes", src.f_w >= dst.w, x alignment).  It is the only path
  that can scan out a foreign dma-buf: decon_map_ion_handle() ->
  ion_iovmm_map() BUG_ON()s on non-ION exporters
  (drivers/staging/android/ion/ion.c:2643), so a panfrost buffer must never go
  through decon_set_win_buffer().
  decon_export_set_win_config() is the fb/ION-free descriptor translation of
  decon_set_win_config(): window enable bits, colour fill, alpha setup,
  bandwidth vote, and a hard -EINVAL on scaling.

Probe split and fb0 lifetime
  decon_probe() is now decon_probe_common(pdev, register_fb).  KMS binds
  samsung,exynos5-decon_driver itself, so the vendor probe never runs in a KMS
  image and decon_kms_get() stands the controller up through the same body
  with register_fb == false (clocks, IRQ, media entity/panel hand-off,
  windows, update kthread, pm_runtime - no framebuffer).
  register_framebuffer() moves from the middle of probe to the tail, after the
  update kthread, pm_runtime_enable() and the panel hand-off, so an fb0 client
  can no longer race a half-initialised DECON; decon->fb_registered records it
  and decon_remove() only unregisters when it was registered.
  int51f: the option-A hand-off branch was removed from the vendor probe
  (the KMS driver binds the node itself); registration stays in place.  The
  weak stub in the shim returns -ENODEV, so a plain fbdev image is unaffected.

Vblank
  decon_int_irq_handler() calls an optionally registered KMS callback outside
  decon->slock on the FRAME interrupt.  The DRM vblank code takes its own
  locks afterwards and never takes decon->slock, so the order is acyclic.

Exports added: decon_export_{acquire,release}_windows, regs_alloc/free,
set_win_buffer, regs_param, regs_param_addr, update_regs, set_win_config,
get/set/put_clocks, dev, plus the decon_kms_* layer A entry points and the
weak decon_kms_attach().

Build: drivers/video/exynos/decon_7580/ 0 errors, no new warnings (the
-Wint-in-bool-context warning at decon_core.c and the unused exynos5_dsim[]
table in dsim_drv.c are pre-existing and untouched).
Probe failure reporting
  Four probe paths returned 0 after a failure (regs mapping, debugfs root,
  ion_client_create, missing media device).  decon_kms_get() must be able to
  fail so the fbdev fallback can bind, so those paths now set ret = -ENODEV
  before their existing unwind.  The success path is untouched.

---

